<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela alkylate production to rise in July.</title>
<headline>Venezuela alkylate production to rise in July.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's state oil subsidiary Maraven plans to increase output of alkylates from its 305,000 barrel per day (bpd) Punta Cardon refinery by the end of July, the company said in a statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The refinery's ageing alkylate plant is being restored to its original design capacity of 540 tonnes per day, it said, without giving previous output figures.</p>
<p>Alkylate is a key component in unleaded, low-benzene gasoline of the type used in the United States.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Ashby, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2611))</p>
